hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17813","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: One who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me."
"17814","And from Ibn Abi Layla that he heard 'Amr ibn Kharijah, Layth said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us while upon his she-camel and said: Verily charity is not lawful for me nor for my household, and he took a hair from the hump of his she-camel and said: Nor what equals this or what weighs this. May Allah curse whoever claims to other than his father or allies other than his patrons. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Indeed Allah gave every possessor of a right his right, and there is no bequest for an heir."
"17815","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun said, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from 'Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Mina while upon his mount, and it was chewing its cud and its saliva was flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Indeed Allah has apportioned for every person his share of inheritance, so no bequest is permissible for an heir. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Verily, whoever claims to other than his father or allies other than his patrons, out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people. Ibn Ja'far said: And Yazid said: And Matar said: And neither sarf nor 'adl will be accepted from him, or 'adl nor sarf. My father said: Yazid said in his hadith: Nor 'adl. Indeed 'Amr ibn Kharijah narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them upon his mount."
"17816","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from 'Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: I was holding the rein of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was chewing its cud and its saliva was flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Indeed Allah Almighty gave every possessor of a right his right, and there is no bequest for an heir. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And whoever claims to other than his father or attaches to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people. 'Affan said: And Hammam added in it with this chain and Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm was not mentioned, and: I was beneath the fore-neck of his mount. And he added in it: Neither 'adl nor sarf will be accepted from him. And in the hadith of Hammam: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed and said: Out of aversion to them."
"17817","'Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from 'Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed while upon his she-camel, and I was beneath its fore-neck, and it was chewing its cud and its saliva was flowing between my shoulders. He said: Indeed Allah Almighty gave every possessor of a right his right, and there is no bequest for an heir. And the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And whoever claims to other than his father or attaches to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; neither sarf nor 'adl will be accepted from him."
"17818","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from 'Amr ibn Kharijah al-Thumali, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the sacrificial animal that is injured, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Slaughter it and dye its sandal in its blood and strike it upon its side, or he said: Upon its flank, and do not eat anything from it, neither you nor the people of your company."
"17819","Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from 'Amr al-Thumali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent sacrificial animals with me and said: If any of them is injured, slaughter it, then strike its sandal in its blood, then strike its side with it, and do not eat, neither you nor the people of your company, and leave it between it and the people."
"17820","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah, informed us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, that 'Amr ibn Kharijah al-Khushani narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them upon his mount, and his mount was chewing its cud and its saliva was flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Indeed Allah Almighty apportioned for every person his share of inheritance, and no bequest for an heir is permissible. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Verily, whoever claims to other than his father or allies other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; Allah will not accept from him sarf nor 'adl, or 'adl nor sarf."
"17821","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from 'Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us while at Mina upon his mount, and I was beneath the fore-neck of his she-camel, and it was chewing its cud and its saliva was flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Indeed Allah Almighty has apportioned for every person his share of inheritance, and no bequest for an heir is permissible. Verily, the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Verily, whoever claims to other than his father or allies other than his patrons, out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people."
"17822","Sa'id said: And Matar narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from 'Amr ibn Kharijah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it, and Matar added in the hadith: And neither sarf nor 'adl will be accepted from him."
"17823","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, and he mentioned the hadith, and he said: Matar said: And neither sarf nor 'adl will be accepted from him."
